WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:03.134
What's up guys?
This is Peter.

00:00:03.134 --> 00:00:06.253
I got back from India
and Pakistan a few months ago.

00:00:06.253 --> 00:00:08.990
Made video series on both countries

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.604
and the number one question
I've received is,

00:00:11.604 --> 00:00:15.122
"What are the differences and the
similarities between India and Pakistan?"

00:00:15.122 --> 00:00:18.450
So that's what I'm gonna
get into here in this video.

00:00:18.866 --> 00:00:21.121
One caveat, I'm a foreigner.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:24.110
I'm not from either country,
haven't lived in either country.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:27.169
I was two weeks in each country.

00:00:28.146 --> 00:00:30.546
So let's start with the differences.

00:00:30.938 --> 00:00:31.938
Police.

00:00:32.055 --> 00:00:34.727
I have no idea what happens psychologically

00:00:34.727 --> 00:00:39.494
when an Indian policeman
puts on that tan police uniform.

00:00:40.126 --> 00:00:42.304
Something happens with ego.

00:00:42.304 --> 00:00:44.101
Some weird complex comes to the surface

00:00:44.101 --> 00:00:49.255
because typically, the Indian police
aren't the best to deal with.

00:00:49.255 --> 00:00:54.749
Now I had no issues, no problems,
but they're not so approachable, I'd say.

00:00:54.749 --> 00:00:57.952
Now this isn't everyone, I'm sure
there are some great cops in India.

00:00:57.952 --> 00:01:01.536
But the over reaching theme was
police are not that cool.

00:01:01.845 --> 00:01:04.929
Pakistan, totally different.

00:01:04.929 --> 00:01:06.740
This was really interesting

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.811
that the police would
go out of their way to help.

00:01:09.811 --> 00:01:14.397
The Rangers,
which guard the borders for the most part,

00:01:14.397 --> 00:01:16.590
super friendly, super approachable.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:21.243
So completely different vibe
with the police in both countries.

00:01:21.488 --> 00:01:26.361
Color, India's so much more
of a colorful country.

00:01:26.963 --> 00:01:29.163
So I think part of that
comes from Hinduism.

00:01:29.163 --> 00:01:31.080
You see a lot of reds,
you see a lot of oranges,

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:32.759
you see a lot of greens.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.765
Also in the women,
because they're colorfully.

00:01:36.765 --> 00:01:40.471
Pakistan, of course there are colors
but just not as much as India.

00:01:40.471 --> 00:01:42.271
Lot of green, lot of black.

00:01:42.385 --> 00:01:46.225
Women, many more women
on the streets in India than Pakistan.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.246
And this really changes too

00:01:49.246 --> 00:01:53.972
when you get to the KPK,
up in the northwest territory of Pakistan.

00:01:53.972 --> 00:01:58.965
City of Peshawar,
really very few women on the streets.

00:01:58.965 --> 00:02:01.837
So it's regionalized
but as a basic rule of thumb,

00:02:01.837 --> 00:02:04.730
many more women on the streets in India.

00:02:05.066 --> 00:02:08.694
Scams... Scams exist in both countries.

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:11.014
I got ripped off in Pakistan
by a taxi driver.

00:02:11.014 --> 00:02:13.118
Also a guy at the hotel
borrowed some money,

00:02:13.118 --> 00:02:17.390
didn't seem too keen
on paying me back, but that was it.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:18.774
India is a different story.

00:02:18.774 --> 00:02:22.037
India in the tourist places
is a much different story.

00:02:22.037 --> 00:02:25.191
So I guess it's
because of years of tourism.

00:02:25.191 --> 00:02:26.907
I don't know what it is but it just seems

00:02:26.907 --> 00:02:30.017
you have to watch
your money closer in India.

00:02:30.704 --> 00:02:31.870
There are people...

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:35.083
There are all sorts of touts,
there are all sorts of little games

00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:37.284
to get money out of you and...

00:02:37.284 --> 00:02:42.760
Not everyone, I was in Jaipur,
some sweet guy gave me some desserts.

00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:46.577
It's not all Indians,
but much more scamming going on in India.

00:02:46.764 --> 00:02:49.664
Homeless,
both countries have homeless people.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:54.029
I'd say that India has many more
that you see out in the streets

00:02:54.029 --> 00:02:56.613
and also more stray dogs.

00:02:57.263 --> 00:03:01.704
Wealthy, both countries have
a minority that is very wealthy

00:03:01.704 --> 00:03:03.110
but it's very different.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:07.079
So in Pakistan,
it seemed like the wealthy were

00:03:07.079 --> 00:03:09.450
far removed on the outskirts of the cities.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:14.109
High walls, barbed wire,
motorcades going by

00:03:14.109 --> 00:03:19.245
creating traffic for everyone else
as these so called "VIPs" went through

00:03:19.245 --> 00:03:20.912
and I think Pakistan...

00:03:20.912 --> 00:03:23.104
You know, you take a city like Karachi,
six years ago was

00:03:23.104 --> 00:03:25.247
the fifth most dangerous city in the world.

00:03:25.247 --> 00:03:26.583
So they say.

00:03:26.583 --> 00:03:31.825
There are a lot more danger factors
I would say for the wealthy in Pakistan.

00:03:31.825 --> 00:03:34.076
I don't know if that's that way now or not.

00:03:34.076 --> 00:03:36.376
But in India they intermingle more.

00:03:36.376 --> 00:03:39.654
It's not like they're hanging out
in the streets with the average person but

00:03:39.654 --> 00:03:43.134
you take Mukesh Ambani,
the richest guy in India.

00:03:43.451 --> 00:03:46.955
His skyscraper home
is pretty close to a main street.

00:03:46.955 --> 00:03:48.930
Of course it has security,
tons of security,

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:52.102
and a wall, and all that stuff
but you see that in India more.

00:03:52.102 --> 00:03:55.710
You see, you know,
not all the wealth is pushed out.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.734
It's sort of intermingled in the cities.

00:03:59.095 --> 00:04:00.378
Religion.

00:04:00.378 --> 00:04:06.285
India is 80% Hindu but there are also 
182 million Muslims in the country

00:04:06.285 --> 00:04:07.835
plus many other religions.

00:04:07.835 --> 00:04:11.061
Over 10% of the world's Muslim people
live in India.

00:04:11.061 --> 00:04:14.856
There are almost as many Muslims
in India as there are in Pakistan

00:04:14.856 --> 00:04:21.712
where roughly 95...
98% of the people are Muslim.

00:04:21.712 --> 00:04:24.818
Those were the big differences
that stuck out during my travels.

00:04:24.818 --> 00:04:26.884
Let's go into the similarities.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.966
Interest in one another.

00:04:30.742 --> 00:04:34.198
Both countries seem to be
very curious about the other.

00:04:34.491 --> 00:04:36.823
In my comments from my video series,

00:04:36.823 --> 00:04:41.443
there are two types of people that chime in

00:04:41.758 --> 00:04:43.229
"Thanks for the nice video, Peter."

00:04:43.229 --> 00:04:45.011
"Lovely people, I'm Indian."

00:04:45.011 --> 00:04:46.956
"Love to see a lot of smiles out there."

00:04:46.956 --> 00:04:51.491
"Sadly, lots of negativity
between the two brotherly nations."

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:54.737
"Wish one day will come
when we can explore each other."

00:04:54.737 --> 00:04:56.017
"Loads of love."

00:04:56.137 --> 00:04:57.577
"From India, and peace."

00:04:57.972 --> 00:05:00.025
So you get these types of messages

00:05:00.025 --> 00:05:02.317
or you get these types.

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.690
"F*ckistan, hai, hai."

00:05:05.094 --> 00:05:06.394
"Terrorist country."

00:05:06.527 --> 00:05:10.548
In this video, guaranteed,
when you finish watching it

00:05:10.548 --> 00:05:12.993
go down into the comments
and check this out.

00:05:12.993 --> 00:05:15.326
You'll see exactly what I'm talking.

00:05:15.326 --> 00:05:18.801
It's either on this far end
of the spectrum,

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:20.051
"I love my brothers."

00:05:20.051 --> 00:05:22.917
"I hope one day... Can't wait to see them."

00:05:23.497 --> 00:05:25.251
"Love  to Pakistan."
"Love to India."

00:05:25.251 --> 00:05:26.251
or...

00:05:27.095 --> 00:05:28.135
The opposite.

00:05:29.056 --> 00:05:30.560
Nothing in the middle.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:31.560
Cricket...

00:05:31.827 --> 00:05:32.827
Enough said.

00:05:33.488 --> 00:05:35.976
Cult-like followings in both countries.

00:05:36.103 --> 00:05:40.366
Hospitality, both cultures
are very cool towards foreigners.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.001
It's very easy to meet people.

00:05:42.001 --> 00:05:44.008
Not a problem, either country.

00:05:44.008 --> 00:05:46.742
India's much more accustomed to tourists.

00:05:47.029 --> 00:05:49.460
So maybe you're not
as much of a novelty there

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:53.882
but in Pakistan,
depending where you're at, it's...

00:05:54.558 --> 00:05:56.438
People are gonna
come out more, I would say.

00:05:56.645 --> 00:05:59.013
And then there's a place called Peshawar.

00:05:59.013 --> 00:06:03.399
Peshawar is in
the northwest part of Pakistan

00:06:03.399 --> 00:06:07.791
and that is hospitality
at its highest frequency.

00:06:07.791 --> 00:06:08.885
There's nothing like it.

00:06:08.885 --> 00:06:10.013
I've never seen anything like it.

00:06:10.013 --> 00:06:12.311
Take two steps,
someone brings you in for tea.

00:06:12.311 --> 00:06:15.691
Two more steps, someone says,
"Have some of my fresh bread."

00:06:15.691 --> 00:06:17.440
Two more steps,
a kid comes out and says,

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:18.975
"Thank you for coming to our country."

00:06:18.975 --> 00:06:20.604
CHILD: Thanks for coming.

00:06:20.604 --> 00:06:21.604
-Thank you.

00:06:22.086 --> 00:06:23.525
Thanks for being so cool.

00:06:23.762 --> 00:06:28.090
So Peshawar has been
the gateway to the Indian subcontinent.

00:06:28.571 --> 00:06:31.350
Lots of conflict has come through the area.

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:33.316
So I was told the people are very...

00:06:33.316 --> 00:06:34.836
They're passionate.

00:06:35.053 --> 00:06:39.669
They're lovers if you come in
in a friendly way

00:06:39.669 --> 00:06:45.180
but they're ruthless warriors
if you come in a not so friendly way.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:48.710
So come in to Peshawar with love

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:53.254
and you will see love and hospitality
like no other place on the planet.

00:06:53.772 --> 00:06:56.818
Regionalized, both countries
are very much regionalized.

00:06:56.818 --> 00:06:59.172
So in India, you have Kerala in the South.

00:06:59.172 --> 00:07:03.341
You have Dehradun, you know,
the foothills of the Himalayas.

00:07:03.341 --> 00:07:04.951
Two completely separate worlds.

00:07:04.951 --> 00:07:07.851
Same with Pakistan,
Hunza Valley and Karachi.

00:07:08.158 --> 00:07:09.500
People are totally different.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.396
Culture is totally different.

00:07:11.612 --> 00:07:12.612
Everything's different.

00:07:12.612 --> 00:07:15.307
What's super interesting is...

00:07:15.307 --> 00:07:18.989
You'll see in the border region,
sometimes the cultures bleed a little bit.

00:07:18.989 --> 00:07:22.813
They bleed together, for example,
Lahore, Amristsar.

00:07:22.813 --> 00:07:28.114
All Punjab people
and the people in Lahore have, in ways,

00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:32.567
more in common with
the people across the border in India

00:07:32.567 --> 00:07:37.756
than they do with another city
in Pakistan like Peshawar.

00:07:38.651 --> 00:07:40.421
I found that to be really cool.

00:07:40.421 --> 00:07:43.533
So regionalized within each country
but then also

00:07:43.533 --> 00:07:48.394
regions of each country
that have a lot in common.

00:07:48.814 --> 00:07:50.347
Alcohol, drugs.

00:07:50.347 --> 00:07:53.941
I know we're in the similarities category
but let me explain.

00:07:53.941 --> 00:07:57.021
So in India there are states like Goa.

00:07:57.021 --> 00:07:58.725
Goa, there's plenty of alcohol.

00:07:58.725 --> 00:08:00.847
Everywhere there are nightclubs,
whatever you want.

00:08:01.242 --> 00:08:03.549
And then there are dry states like Kerala.

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:07.657
Where I don't think you can buy it
in markets or on the streets.

00:08:07.781 --> 00:08:10.814
In Pakistan,
the whole country, you can't buy it

00:08:10.814 --> 00:08:14.054
in markets or on the streets anywhere

00:08:14.054 --> 00:08:16.692
but the similarities are it does exist

00:08:16.692 --> 00:08:21.678
and there are underground party scenes
in all the big Pakistani cities.

00:08:21.678 --> 00:08:22.693
That's for sure.

00:08:22.693 --> 00:08:23.675
It exists.

00:08:23.675 --> 00:08:25.425
People are gonna say it doesn't.

00:08:25.425 --> 00:08:28.919
They don't want it to exist,
but the reality is it does exist.

00:08:29.217 --> 00:08:30.534
At what level, I don't know.

00:08:30.534 --> 00:08:32.063
I didn't spend a long enough time there.

00:08:32.087 --> 00:08:35.046
And more interestingly was...

00:08:35.046 --> 00:08:36.406
Were the opiates.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:41.061
So I saw in India,
in the villages, people...

00:08:41.895 --> 00:08:44.964
It was like a mild form of opium I believe.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.970
They were drinking.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:50.824
And then hashish
on the streets in Pakistan.

00:08:51.592 --> 00:08:53.442
Now these are only two instances I saw.

00:08:53.442 --> 00:08:56.047
I don't know how frequent this stuff is.

00:08:56.081 --> 00:09:00.710
Architecture, so where I saw
the similarities were in Punjab.

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:02.650
You have Mughal architecture.

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:07.062
Lahore, beautiful, stunning,
Mughal architecture in Lahore

00:09:07.062 --> 00:09:11.118
and that also carries over
to Delhi, Taj Mahal.

00:09:11.544 --> 00:09:13.671
Beautiful Moghul architecture.

00:09:14.146 --> 00:09:18.430
There are some common threads
depending where you are in the countries.

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:19.640
Complex.

00:09:20.189 --> 00:09:25.246
You could spend a lifetime
studying the cultural nuances,

00:09:25.246 --> 00:09:28.671
the history, geography, the politics.

00:09:28.671 --> 00:09:32.437
There is so much going on in each place.

00:09:33.039 --> 00:09:34.719
Cut off from one another.

00:09:35.022 --> 00:09:38.888
Most Pakistanis cannot go to India,
most Indians cannot go to Pakistan.

00:09:38.888 --> 00:09:40.057
There are some exceptions.

00:09:40.057 --> 00:09:44.790
Some visas for family members,
or business men, but it's not easy.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.752
Most people will never see the other side.

00:09:48.152 --> 00:09:49.752
That benefits the politicians.

00:09:49.752 --> 00:09:51.812
That benefits the media.

00:09:51.812 --> 00:09:53.541
It doesn't benefit the people.

00:09:53.541 --> 00:09:56.610
'Cause if the people
actually got to intermingle more,

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.954
they got to hang out,
a lot know this already,

00:09:58.954 --> 00:10:02.283
but they'd realize
how much common ground there is

00:10:02.283 --> 00:10:04.424
and there's no need
to really fear each other.

00:10:04.932 --> 00:10:07.176
Easy for me to say, I'm an outsider.

00:10:07.176 --> 00:10:10.931
I'm not talking about the bloody history,
I'm talking about 2020

00:10:10.931 --> 00:10:15.837
and the fact that
most people are cool on both sides

00:10:15.837 --> 00:10:18.553
and the fact that they can't intermingle

00:10:18.553 --> 00:10:21.172
does not help either country
in the long run.

00:10:21.239 --> 00:10:23.160
Patriotism, pride.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:26.305
There's a lot of pride in both countries.

00:10:26.305 --> 00:10:28.020
Very strong pride on both sides.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:33.484
The best manifestation of this
is the Wagah border crossing.

00:10:34.259 --> 00:10:40.384
It's this crazy dynamic
of machismo, ballet, patriotism.

00:10:41.252 --> 00:10:43.793
It's super interesting,
I made a video on it actually.

00:10:43.793 --> 00:10:46.858
But yeah, both sides
have a super patriotic element,

00:10:46.858 --> 00:10:48.720
nationalistic element too,

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:50.434
and then there's a whole other demographic

00:10:50.434 --> 00:10:55.754
that just really does not care
about the political tension

00:10:55.754 --> 00:10:58.683
or if they think their country
is better than the other one.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:02.046
India and Pakistan,
some of the gems of Planet Earth.

00:11:02.046 --> 00:11:04.714
If you have the chance,
go to both of them.

00:11:04.714 --> 00:11:07.441
It's really interesting
to do a compare and contrast.

00:11:07.441 --> 00:11:10.268
I'm just scratching the surface
with this video.

00:11:10.268 --> 00:11:11.263
I know it.

00:11:11.263 --> 00:11:13.786
If you want to see more
about both countries

00:11:13.786 --> 00:11:16.545
then go down below into the description.

00:11:16.545 --> 00:11:17.703
I made series.

00:11:17.703 --> 00:11:20.366
I have links for series on both countries

00:11:20.366 --> 00:11:22.886
and also if you want to
support this channel

00:11:22.886 --> 00:11:27.397
please go, again, down into
the link below, description below,

00:11:27.397 --> 00:11:30.533
and you'll see links there
to support the channel.

00:11:30.615 --> 00:11:31.976
Hope you enjoyed that.

00:11:31.976 --> 00:11:33.153
Hope you get to go.

00:11:33.153 --> 00:11:36.659
If you're from either one of the countries
I just mentioned, India or Pakistan,

00:11:36.659 --> 00:11:38.526
loved it, thank you so much.

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:40.660
Fantastic experiences.

00:11:42.005 --> 00:11:43.799
Hope to see you in the next video.

00:11:43.799 --> 00:11:45.319
[children giggling]

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:48.323
MAN: Thank you, sir. Thank yo so much.

00:11:48.323 --> 00:11:49.595
Sir, thank you so much.

00:11:49.595 --> 00:11:51.699
PETER: Thank you, thank you, bye-bye.

00:11:51.699 --> 00:11:53.375
-You guys are so cool.
-You are so very cool.

00:11:53.375 --> 00:11:55.588
-You guys are
very welcoming, very friendly.

00:11:55.588 --> 00:11:56.588
-Thank you.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:58.190
-Big hearts.

00:11:58.714 --> 00:12:01.410
-Yeah, big mountains, big hearts.

